<h2 id="convergence-commitments">Convergence by commitment</h2>

<p>The RCE thesis rests on seven commitments. Each has been reached independently, often more than once, by people working for their own reasons. The tables below list projects whose primary sources (paper, official documentation or repository) were opened and checked against the sentence written here. Each row says what the project established and where it stops relative to the commitment. These are convergence observations: agreement in direction, not confirmation of RCE's claims and not a ranking. Items from OpenIE, the organization behind RCE, are marked <em>same house</em> and are never used as evidence.</p>

<p>Acronyms used in this section: RCE, the Reality Code Engine; AST, abstract syntax tree; IR, intermediate representation; LLM, large language model; JSON, JavaScript Object Notation; WASM, WebAssembly; SMT, satisfiability modulo theories (Z3 is an SMT solver); DST, deterministic simulation testing; CEGIS, counterexample-guided inductive synthesis.</p>

