<h3 id="cc4">4. Store intent; derive the implementation</h3>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto"><table class={tbl}>
  <thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it established</th><th>Where it stops</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>FORTRAN, Backus et al., 1957; deductive synthesis, Manna and Waldinger, 1980 [C29; C30]</td><td>Automatic coding from formulas; programs extracted from constructive proofs</td><td>FORTRAN became a compiler; deductive synthesis had no implementation at the time</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Spec-driven development, as classified by Böckeler [C31]</td><td>Three levels: spec-first, spec-anchored and spec-as-source, in which "the human never touches the code"; of Kiro, spec-kit and Tessl, only Tessl explores spec-as-source</td><td>The spec is natural language; nothing checks that the code is the spec</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Vericoding benchmark, 2025 [C32]</td><td>12,504 formal specifications in Dafny, Verus and Lean; off-the-shelf LLMs succeed on 82%, 44% and 27%; adding natural language did not significantly help</td><td>Specification languages are the proof languages; no runtime form or multi-target emission</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Codifide [C7]</td><td>Every definition carries an intent that compilation never discards</td><td>Contract-and-dispatch scope</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>

<h3 id="cc5">5. The model proposes; a deterministic gate decides</h3>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto"><table class={tbl}>
  <thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it established</th><th>Where it stops</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>CompCert; seL4 [C33; C34]</td><td>Machine-checked compiler and kernel; CompCert checks an unverified heuristic's output with a verified checker; seL4's proof cost about 20 person-years</td><td>Proof effort per artifact</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sketching and CEGIS, Solar-Lezama et al., 2006 [C35]</td><td>A synthesizer proposes, a checker returns a counterexample, and the loop repeats</td><td>Proposers are solvers, not learned models</td></tr>
    <tr><td>AlphaProof; Clover; AutoVerus [C36; C37; C38]</td><td>A model proposes; Lean, Dafny or Verus checks</td><td>Gate on proofs or code text; no canonical program form</td></tr>
