<h3 id="cc-rce">What the RCE project measured (OpenIE's own data)</h3>
<p>The following are OpenIE's own results from <a href="https://research.openie.dev/papers/rce/">the RCE paper</a> (version 1.4), checked against the engine repository. They are reported here as the project's data, not as a comparison with the projects above.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Round trip.</strong> On 10,000 preregistered generated Forms with a frozen engine and no model calls, Form IR to canonical JSON and back was the identity for 10,000 of 10,000. Two compiles gave the same bytes, and the XState and SCXML (State Chart XML) projections of the original and round-tripped Form were byte identical, in 10,000 of 10,000. The emitted Python printed the reference trace in 9,999 of 10,000.</li>
  <li><strong>Five targets.</strong> The Rust, WASM, Python, XState and SCXML targets print the reference trace byte for byte on 529 events (29 edge events and 500 seeded random values) of one eleven-operator specification. This is differential testing on that input set, not a proof and not a 10,000-Form result.</li>
  <li><strong>Canonical form.</strong> The canonical serialization is injective on Forms, so two Forms that differ have different shape hashes. Equivalence of behaviour is defined separately (fit equivalence), and equivalent variants are grouped by sound rewrites in an e-graph; the paper does not claim that equivalent behaviour always yields one canonical form.</li>
  <li><strong>Proofs.</strong> Determinism, totality, replay as a fold of the log, and atomicity of refused events are proved in Lean 4 on a core calculus. The Rust program emitter is proved on a core as a verified translation into MiniRust, a deep embedding of the emitted Rust subset; that the Rust compiler implements MiniRust is trusted and tested. This proof covers the program emitter, not the Form projection.</li>
  <li><strong>Repair ladder, with the location given and token identity as the gate, zero model calls.</strong> 520,541 of 520,821 one-token mutants (99.95%) in nine repositories; 13,586 of 21,320 single-statement Java bugs (63.7%) when the whole file and project indexes are supplied, and 9,288 of 24,072 (38.6%) from the seven-line hunk alone.</li>
  <li><strong>Gate.</strong> Replay of recorded inputs, a shadow run with a coverage bound, an output schema check and a Kani proof certificate; a proposed rewrite also needs a Z3 proof. A local 1.5-billion-parameter model proposed 16 equivalences, of which the gate admitted 3.</li>
  <li><strong>Energy.</strong> Every receipt carries <code>est_j</code>; an unpriced model call is never read as zero. <code>measured_j</code> (wall meter) is empty in every result so far.</li>
</ul>

